<title>CANADA: Canada October retail sales rise 1.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada October retail sales rise 1.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian retail sales rose 1.1 percent in October to a seasonally adjusted C$18.20 billion from an upwardly revised C$18.00 billion (C$17.93 billion) in September, Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>				    Month pct    Year pct    Total</p>
<p>Sales, seasonally adjusted     +1.1	 +3.5     C$18.20 bln</p>
<p>Sales, ex vehicles, s/a	  +0.9	 +3.2     C$13.83 bln</p>
<p>Sales, unadjusted		  n/a	  +7.1     C$18.55 bln</p>
<p>Statistics Canada said early indications for November sales were for a rise.</p>
</text>
